WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.133
Two planets, different speeds.

2
00:00:03.093 --> 00:00:04.993
Look what happens when we draw the connection.

3
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.847
In 1609, German astronomer Johannes Kepler used

4
00:00:09.787 --> 00:00:12.687
Tycho Brahe's measurements of Mars to show that

5
00:00:12.627 --> 00:00:14.427
planets follow oval paths.

6
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.250
One year is one trip around the Sun.

7
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.730
Earth takes about 365 days.

8
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.090
Mars takes 687 Earth days.

9
00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:26.975
Mark both positions at the same moment.

10
00:00:27.715 --> 00:00:30.775
Connect them then repeat at equal time steps.

11
00:00:31.995 --> 00:00:33.635
Here are 15 Earth years.

12
00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:37.982
Beautiful to look at, fun to draw, and a way to

13
00:00:37.922 --> 00:00:39.562
understand how a system works.

14
00:00:40.242 --> 00:00:41.182
Try drawing it together.
